{
  "about": [
    "Shared vectors for the screen matcher: ranking entries against a query and choosing which manifest screens are searchable.",
    "Authored in canopy (tests/canopy_mcp/fixtures/collections/match-vectors.json); every other holder keeps a byte-identical copy.",
    "ASCII-only, no trailing whitespace, one final newline.",
    "Every case has a name, a kind and an expect array. A reader must fail on a kind it does not know; the kinds are rank and include.",
    "Words: split the text on non-alphanumerics, then at lower->Upper, at Upper->Upper+lower and at letter<->digit boundaries, and lower-case each part (LinacView -> linac, view; SR01C -> sr, 01, c).",
    "rank {query, candidates:[{label, keywords[]}], expect:[labels]}: the query is lower-cased and split on whitespace into tokens; no tokens -> no matches. A candidate matches when every token is a prefix of some word of its label or a keyword, or of the joined lower-case words of that label or keyword.",
    "Matches are ordered by: all tokens matched in the label first; then the first token prefixing the first label word; then more label words prefixed by some token; then candidate list order. expect lists the labels of the matches in that order.",
    "include {manifest:[{id, category, kind}], showSubScreens, expect:[ids]}: a screen is searchable when kind is 'ir', category does not start with '@', and showSubScreens is true or the id is not a sub-screen. A sub-screen id has a path segment equal to 'embedded' or a basename starting with '_'. expect keeps manifest order."
  ],
